body:
> Is git::Permissions::all() likely to become an issue?

You are right! It's better to go with the secure defaults for the trust map and only override the pieces that need changing. Maybe like so:

```Rust
let mut options = git_sec::trust::Mapping::default();
options.full.permissions.config = …;
options.reduced.permissions.config = …;
```

It's super valuable to do this as it seems to be easy, even for me, to suggest potentially insecure settings. I am definitely still learning.
